course: dictionary
lesson: 7977
title: Recommend: say it is good, or say what to do
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To recommend something is to say it is good and that someone should try it. To recommend that someone does something is to advise them to do it. «I recommend it» means «I think you will like it».
explain: Look at the words around recommend to tell which meaning fits. «A squash ball is small, so protective eyewear is recommended for squash.» Here it means advised: players should wear eye protection.
explain: «Energy drinks are not recommended for children because of the caffeine in them.» Not recommended means the opposite of advised: it is advised against. The reason comes straight after the sentence, so read on.
explain: Recommend changes its ending: recommends, recommended, recommending. Test your meaning by swapping in «advise» or «suggest as good». If it still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: To recommend means to say something is good, or to advise someone to do something.
fact: «I recommend it» means you think someone will enjoy it.
fact: «Recommended for ages 8+» on a label tells you the age that is advised.
fact: «Recommend that you…» is always followed by advice, such as «recommend that you rest».
fact: When you see «9 out of 10 dentists recommend», ask how many people were asked and who paid for the survey, because a few people prove very little.
exercise: «Highly recommend this book, it is brilliant!» What does recommend mean here? | Warn people to stay away | Read it out loud | Write it down for later | *Say that something is good and you should try it
exercise: «A squash ball is small, so protective eyewear is recommended for squash.» What is recommended here? | *Eye protection, to be worn for safety | A faster game | A squash ball, to buy | Playing outside
exercise: Mum reads a label: «Not recommended for children.» What does it tell her? | *It advises against it for children | It is free for children | Children love it | It must be bought by children
test: Dad says, «I recommend that you wear a helmet.» What does he mean? | He has lost your helmet | *He is advising you to wear a helmet | He is cross about your helmet | He has a helmet for sale
test: «Energy drinks are not recommended for children.» What is the reason the sentence gives? | They taste bad | *They contain caffeine | They are too expensive | Children never drink them
exam: Why do claims like «9 out of 10 dentists recommend» need checking? | Because dentists never recommend anything | Because recommend means something is bad | Because the number 9 is too big | *Because only a few people may have been asked, and who paid matters
